## 5. Where this ticket's changes live

| Change | Procedure | What |
|---|---|---|
| Gap 1 — catch-up window | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew` | `#tbl_DLQ_Installment_Research` population: `BETWEEN @StartDays AND @EndDays` (was `= @StartDays`) |
| Gap 2 — tax-year validation | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew` | Eligibility `EXISTS` check: added `TEMP.CurrentTaxYear = ap.CURRENT_TAX_YEAR` |
| Non-determinism fix (found during testing) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew` | `@DIRTaxYear`/`@DIRInstallmentNo`/`@DIRDueDate` pull: same year-scoping added, so it can't grab a different year's row than the eligibility check just validated |
| Dedup guard installment-blindness fix (found during testing) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` | Guard's matching `SELECT`: added `TaxYear`/`InstallmentNo` to the business key (previously only Loan+Agency+TaxID+PropertyID+LienSEQ+SystemCode) |
| DIR carve-out (11/06) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` | New block inside the guard's `IF @ExistingExceptionID IS NOT NULL`: update in place instead of suppress, when the due date genuinely changed |
| Variable rename (11/11, cosmetic) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` | `@Winner*` → `@Existing*` local variables only |

